    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: The quick brown fox jumped over the **lazy dog.**
      - kind:
          Raw: ""
      - kind:
          Raw: A paragraph __with
      - kind:
          Raw: soft wrapping__ in
      - kind:
          Raw: it.
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 3
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: 3.1 Verbatim
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "Text between verbatim delimiters is preserved literally. A backslash escape applies only to verbatim delimiters; all other text, including backslashes, is preserved. When verbatim content ends with a backslash, place whitespace before the closing delimiter; it is trimmed ("
        children:
          - kind:
              Link: 4.3 Trimming
            attributes:
              - value: "#"
            children:
              - kind:
                  Delimiter: LinkName
                children:
                  - kind:
                      Text: "4.3"
          - kind:
              Text: ).
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "To specify a syntax, a language attribute ("
        children:
          - kind:
              Link: 5.1 Inline Attributes
            attributes:
              - value: "#"
            children:
              - kind:
                  Delimiter: LinkName
                children:
                  - kind:
                      Text: "5.1"
          - kind:
              Text: ") may be attached to the opening delimiter:"
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "Some code with \\``python: print(\"Hello, world!\")\\``"
      - kind:
          Raw: ""
      - kind:
          Raw: "``python:"
      - kind:
          Raw: "def greet(name):"
      - kind:
          Raw: "    print(f\"Hello, {name}!\")"
      - kind:
          Raw: "``"
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: Each line of a verbatim block (
        children:
          - kind:
              Link: 4.1 Blocks
            attributes:
              - value: "#"
            children:
              - kind:
                  Delimiter: LinkName
                children:
                  - kind:
                      Text: "4.1"
          - kind:
              Text: ") is dedented by the whitespace preceding the opening verbatim delimiter:"
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "-"
      - kind:
          Raw: "  A list item"
      - kind:
          Raw: "  ``python:"
      - kind:
          Raw: "  def greet(name):"
      - kind:
          Raw: "    print(f\"Hello, {name}!\")"
      - kind:
          Raw: "  ``"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-"
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "When parsed, the remaining whitespace is preserved:"
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: python
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "def greet(name):"
      - kind:
          Raw: "  print(f\"Hello, {name}!\")"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 3
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: 3.2 Tables
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "Tables are constructed using table header "
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: Verbatim
            children:
              - kind:
                  Raw: "#|"
          - kind:
              Text: " and table row "
          - kind:
              Delimiter: Verbatim
            children:
              - kind:
                  Raw: "-|"
          - kind:
              Text: " delimiters. Within a row, cells are delimited using table cell "
          - kind:
              Delimiter: Verbatim
            children:
              - kind:
                  Raw: "||"
          - kind:
              Text: ". Each cell may include semantic delimiters. A table is terminated by a blank line ("
          - kind:
              Link: 1.2 Whitespace and Blank Lines
            attributes:
              - value: "#"
            children:
              - kind:
                  Delimiter: LinkName
                children:
                  - kind:
                      Text: "1.2"
          - kind:
              Text: ).
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "#| Name       || Type      || Color    ||"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-| Apple      || Fruit     || Red      ||"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-| **Carrot** || Vegetable || Orange   ||"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-| Blueberry  || Fruit     || Blue     ||"
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: Table rows may share a line.
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "#| Name || Type || Color || -| Banana || Fruit || Yellow ||"
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: Table rows are not required to have the same number of cells. The number of columns in a table is determined by the row with the most cells. Missing cells are parsed as empty.
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "#| Name       || Type      || Color    ||"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-| Apple      || Fruit     ||"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-| Carrot     || Vegetable || Orange   || Crunchy ||"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-| Blueberry  || Fruit     || Blue     ||"
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "Tables may begin without a header:"
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "-| Apple      || Fruit     ||"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-| Carrot     || Vegetable || Orange   || Crunchy ||"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-| Blueberry  || Fruit     || Blue     ||"
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "Tables may have multiple header rows in any position:"
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "#|            ||           ||          || Texture ||"
      - kind:
          Raw: "#| Name       || Type      || Color    ||"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-| Apple      || Fruit     ||"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-| Blueberry  || Fruit     || Blue     ||"
      - kind:
          Raw: "#| Vegetables ||"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-| Carrot     || Vegetable || Orange   || Crunchy ||"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 3
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: 3.3 Links
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "A link is either a hyperlink "
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: Verbatim
            children:
              - kind:
                  Raw: "[[ ]]"
          - kind:
              Text: " or a slot link "
          - kind:
              Delimiter: Verbatim
            children:
              - kind:
                  Raw: "<< >>"
          - kind:
              Text: ". A hyperlink is a reference the reader may follow to another resource. A slot link is filled by its target, such as an image or template variable. Links are inline only; no block form of either kind is valid."
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "- [[https://kdl.dev]]"
      - kind:
          Raw: "- [[spec.mg]]"
      - kind:
          Raw: ""
      - kind:
          Raw: "- <<embedded-img.png>>"
      - kind:
          Raw: "- <<my-note.mg>>"
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: Attributes (
        children:
          - kind:
              Link: 5.1 Inline Attributes
            attributes:
              - value: "#"
            children:
              - kind:
                  Delimiter: LinkName
                children:
                  - kind:
                      Text: "5.1"
          - kind:
              Text: ") on links conventionally declare the target's namespace:"
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "- [[#: 3.3 Links]]      heading namespace"
      - kind:
          Raw: "- <<$:note.mg>>         project root namespace"
      - kind:
          Raw: "- [[spell:Fireball]]    spell namespace"
      - kind:
          Raw: "- <<ingredient:tomato>> ingredient namespace"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 3
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: 3.4 Annotations
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "Annotations are alias "
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: Verbatim
            children:
              - kind:
                  Raw: (( ))
          - kind:
              Text: " and note "
          - kind:
              Delimiter: Verbatim
            children:
              - kind:
                  Raw: "{{ }}"
          - kind:
              Text: " nodes. An alias carries an alternate name or creates a named anchor point. A note is for any attached context such as footnotes and comments."
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "Annotations are commonly attached to links:"
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "- [[https://kdl.dev]]((KDL doc site))"
      - kind:
          Raw: "- [[https://kdl.dev]]{{"
      - kind:
          Raw: "    KDL is a small, pleasant document language with XML-like node..."
      - kind:
          Raw: "  }}"
      - kind:
          Raw: "- [[https://kdl.dev]]((KDL doc site)){{a cuddly document language}}"
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "Annotations can attach to a span or another annotation:"
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "- ::Groceries::{{ needed for [[marinara sauce]] }}"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-- ::tomato::((San Marzano tomato))"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-- olive oil"
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "When an annotation appears inline with no preceding delimiter to attach to, an anchor is registered at its position. For notes the anchor is indexed by document order:"
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: A good marinara starts with San Marzano
      - kind:
          Raw: "tomato{{ A tomato is a fruit not a vegetable }} and a generous amount"
      - kind:
          Raw: of olive oil.
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "The prior example's note is indexed as "
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: Verbatim
            children:
              - kind:
                  Raw: "1"
          - kind:
              Text: ". When the annotation is an alias or note with attached alias, the anchor is keyed by the alias name:"
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "A good marinara starts with {{ A tomato is a fruit not a vegetable }}((San Marzano tomato))"
      - kind:
          Raw: and a generous amount of olive oil.
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "An alias annotation may be used to name an anchor point for a following note to target:"
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: A good marinara starts with ((San Marzano tomato)) and a generous
      - kind:
          Raw: amount of olive oil.
      - kind:
          Raw: ""
      - kind:
          Raw: "{{ A fruit not a vegetable }}((San Marzano tomato))"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 2
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: 4 Boundaries
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 3
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: 4.1 Blocks
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: A marker or delimiter on an otherwise blank line opens a block. A block is terminated by the same marker or delimiter with no attributes (
        children:
          - kind:
              Link: 5 Attributes
            attributes:
              - value: "#"
            children:
              - kind:
                  Delimiter: LinkName
                children:
                  - kind:
                      Text: "5"
          - kind:
              Text: ) on an otherwise blank line.
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "**"
      - kind:
          Raw: The quick brown fox jumped over the lazy dog.
      - kind:
          Raw: "**"
      - kind:
          Raw: ""
      - kind:
          Raw: "# Reading notes"
      - kind:
          Raw: "--"
      - kind:
          Raw: "Chapter 3 was particularly relevant:"
      - kind:
          Raw: " >"
      - kind:
          Raw: " __"
      - kind:
          Raw: "  quote from chapter 3"
      - kind:
          Raw: " __"
      - kind:
          Raw: " >"
      - kind:
          Raw: "--"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 3
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: 4.2 Free
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "A free node has no inherent semantic type. It exists as a structural building block which carries attributes and annotations. The free marker "
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: Verbatim
            children:
              - kind:
                  Raw: "="
          - kind:
              Text: " denotes a line or block; the free delimiter "
          - kind:
              Delimiter: Verbatim
            children:
              - kind:
                  Raw: "::"
          - kind:
              Text: " marks a span."
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "= A free line"
      - kind:
          Raw: ""
      - kind:
          Raw: "="
      - kind:
          Raw: " A free block"
      - kind:
          Raw: ""
      - kind:
          Raw: " can group content across lines"
      - kind:
          Raw: "="
      - kind:
          Raw: ""
      - kind:
          Raw: "The sauce needs ::San Marzano::((a plum tomato))."
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 3
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: 4.3 Trimming
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "Whitespace is not used to structure Mog syntax. Leading and trailing whitespace is trimmed when parsing a document. The following headings parse identically:"
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "# My heading"
      - kind:
          Raw: "  # My heading  "
      - kind:
          Raw: "      #     My heading  "
      - kind:
          Raw: "#My heading          "
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "Leading and trailing whitespace is trimmed within semantic delimiters, except for verbatim content, which is trimmed only at its delimiters; each contained line is dedented, not trimmed ("
        children:
          - kind:
              Link: 3.1 Verbatim
            attributes:
              - value: "#"
            children:
              - kind:
                  Delimiter: LinkName
                children:
                  - kind:
                      Text: "3.1"
          - kind:
              Text: "). The following bold text spans contain the same parsed content:"
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "**    bold statement**"
      - kind:
          Raw: "**bold statement    **"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 3
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: 4.4 Escapes
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "A backslash escapes the character or run of repeated characters that follows. Backslashes are the exception: "
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: Verbatim
            children:
              - kind:
                  Raw: "\\\\"
          - kind:
              Text: " escapes a single backslash, never a run. Within verbatim content, only a verbatim delimiter is escaped ("
          - kind:
              Link: 3.1 Verbatim
            attributes:
              - value: "#"
            children:
              - kind:
                  Delimiter: LinkName
                children:
                  - kind:
                      Text: "3.1"
          - kind:
              Text: ).
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "\\**this is not bold\\**"
      - kind:
          Raw: "\\\\**this is bold**"
      - kind:
          Raw: "\\\\\\**this is not bold\\**"
      - kind:
          Raw: ""
      - kind:
          Raw: "\\### this is not a heading"
      - kind:
          Raw: "\\---- this is not a list item"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 2
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: 5 Attributes
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: Attributes attach generic KDL v2 data to nodes. An attribute can attach inline or as a block. Inline attributes are terminated with a colon.
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 3
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: 5.1 Inline Attributes
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "Inline attributes are KDL Nodes, separated and terminated by a colon "
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: Verbatim
            children:
              - kind:
                  Raw: ":"
          - kind:
              Text: ". Each attribute may have a tag, name, and value. In a KDL Document, "
          - kind:
              Delimiter: Verbatim
            children:
              - kind:
                  Raw: key=value
          - kind:
              Text: " represents a node property. For Mog's inline attributes an equals "
          - kind:
              Delimiter: Verbatim
            children:
              - kind:
                  Raw: "="
          - kind:
              Text: " instead names the node. This allows inline and verbatim attributes ("
          - kind:
              Link: 5.2 Verbatim Attributes
            attributes:
              - value: "#"
            children:
              - kind:
                  Delimiter: LinkName
                children:
                  - kind:
                      Text: "5.2"
          - kind:
              Text: ) to interoperate.
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "-size=medium: T-Shirt"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-"
      - kind:
          Raw: " ``attr:"
      - kind:
          Raw: " size large"
      - kind:
          Raw: " ``"
      - kind:
          Raw: " Vintage T-Shirt with a block of text for its backstory"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-"
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "Both of these shirt notes carry a size attribute of the same format. If the first T-Shirt was converted into a block using "
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: Verbatim
            children:
              - kind:
                  Raw: size medium
          - kind:
              Text: " to store size, the representation of data is the same."
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: Additional attributes may be added as a chain beginning from the terminating colon of the prior attribute. Attribute chains must stay on the same line as their parent. A newline or whitespace character marks the beginning of text content.
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "-info: Item with \"info\" attribute"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-info:green: Attribute chain"
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "When a node has multiple attributes that share a key or tag, the values can be comma "
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: Verbatim
            children:
              - kind:
                  Raw: ","
          - kind:
              Text: " separated. Key and tag are repeated for each repeated value:"
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "-(season)fall,winter:size=medium,small: Knit Beanie"
      - kind:
          Raw: ""
      - kind:
          Raw: "## Equivalent Attributes"
      - kind:
          Raw: "-(season)fall:(season)winter:size=medium:size=small: Knit Beanie"
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 3
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: 5.2 Verbatim Attributes
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "Verbatim attributes are declared by attaching an "
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: Verbatim
            children:
              - kind:
                  Raw: attr
          - kind:
              Text: " attribute to an opening verbatim delimiter. A verbatim attribute is parsed as a KDL Document, then attached to the containing node. At the top level, the containing node is the document."
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "``attr:"
      - kind:
          Raw: "title \"My Document\""
      - kind:
          Raw: "authors \"John Doe\""
      - kind:
          Raw: "``"
      - kind:
          Raw: ""
      - kind:
          Raw: "="
      - kind:
          Raw: "``attr:"
      - kind:
          Raw: "title \"My Node\""
      - kind:
          Raw: "authors \"Also John Doe\""
      - kind:
          Raw: "``"
      - kind:
          Raw: "="
  - kind:
      Marker:
        depth: 3
        kind: Heading
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: 5.3 Duplicate Attributes
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "When attributes share the same name they are not deduplicated. Instead, all attributes are stored in document order."
  - kind:
      Delimiter: Verbatim
    attributes:
      - value: mog
    children:
      - kind:
          Raw: "``attr:"
      - kind:
          Raw: "authors \"John\""
      - kind:
          Raw: "``"
      - kind:
          Raw: ""
      - kind:
          Raw: "-authors=James:authors=Jamie: Item"
      - kind:
          Raw: ""
      - kind:
          Raw: "``attr:"
      - kind:
          Raw: "authors \"Jane\""
      - kind:
          Raw: "``"
  - kind: Paragraph
    children:
      - kind:
          Text: "This document has two "
        children:
          - kind:
              Delimiter: Verbatim
            children:
              - kind:
                  Raw: authors
          - kind:
              Text: " attributes, "
          - kind:
              Delimiter: Verbatim
            children:
              - kind:
                  Raw: John
          - kind:
              Text: " and "
          - kind:
              Delimiter: Verbatim
            children:
              - kind:
                  Raw: Jane
          - kind:
              Text: ". The list node additionally has two separate "
          - kind:
              Delimiter: Verbatim
            children:
              - kind:
                  Raw: authors
          - kind:
              Text: " attributes, "
          - kind:
              Delimiter: Verbatim
            children:
              - kind:
                  Raw: James
          - kind:
              Text: " and "
          - kind:
              Delimiter: Verbatim
            children:
              - kind:
                  Raw: Jamie
          - kind:
              Text: ". Attributes with duplicate names are not merged or overridden."
